cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GrTools in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GrTools.jl: a next-generation Julia toolkit for black-hole perturbation theory"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "GrTools contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-14
abstract: >-
  GrTools is a next-generation suite of Julia packages for black-hole
  perturbation theory:
  Kerr geometry, spin-weighted spherical and spheroidal harmonics, the
  Teukolsky equation (radial solutions, point-particle fluxes, quasinormal
  and quadratic-quasinormal modes), metric reconstruction, gravitational and
  scalar self-force, post-Newtonian expansions, EMRI waveforms, and
  relativistic accretion-disc modes. All numerical paths are type-generic:
  BigFloat inputs inherit the active working precision end-to-end.
keywords:
  - black-hole perturbation theory
  - Teukolsky equation
  - self-force
  - EMRI
  - gravitational waves
  - Julia
license: MIT
